Let $u:=\partial_x\Phi_\nu$, which is continuous, with $\partial_xu$ and $\partial_x^2u$ continuous and bounded, and which solves, for almost every $v$,
\begin{equation}\label{e.magnetization.pde}
 -\partial_vu=\partial_x^2u+2\zeta_\nu\,u\,\partial_xu,
\end{equation}
